    "proximate_text": "The cause of this event was the main generator's AQR being active and attempting to maintain the reactive power setpoint following a 100 percent load rejection and in island mode operation. The AQR is not designed to be used as a voltage control method when the plant is disconnected from the grid.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "Design/control-software deficiency allowing improper voltage-regulation mode during island operation",
    "provisional": true
